# NOTE: composer.lock is deliberately NOT ignored here — this repo commits it by
# S440 law (see b6b44e8 and tests/SecurityAuditCheckTest.php's
# testTheCommittedLockExists); the reference's own /composer.lock line is the
# known family contradiction, kept out on purpose, not an oversight.

# Per-checkout agent tooling and state — never part of a plugin package.
# The plugins catalog checksums codeload archive/<ref>.tar.gz bytes, so tracked
# agent state makes the distributed tarball — and every catalog pin — churn on
# each caliber rewrite, and installs receive junk.
.caliber/
.claude/
.opencode/
.remember/
CALIBER_LEARNINGS.md
